  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "Bounded downstream source changes",
      "finding": "The BuildQuery auditor and runtime constructor each change only the new3 preparation branch to new3-retry1; retained new4 and existing63 branches remain exact. The runtime auditor additionally binds the successor constructor's precise canonical name, 12,707-byte size and D6A9 hash. The observed input helper's five edits select the retry preparation/configuration, the A04C auditor name/size and a separate Root retry source review. Every other source byte reverses to its accepted baseline; all thirty full-line helper bodies are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "area": "Original attempt preserved",
      "finding": "All fifteen original prepared files plus the original buildquery-launch.json retain exact bytes. Root CB6 catalog acceptance, independent 9712 negative, Root 1A6 acceptance and eleven original negative-input versions were rehashed. The original rejection remains three granted groups, one attempted, two unstarted and zero native owners, metadata or tests. Those immutable accepted closure records supply provenance; this peer performs no new process-absence audit and transfers no outcome to the retry."
    },
    {
      "area": "Clone admission and mutation boundary",
      "finding": "The new cloner requires an exact contained Root configuration/hash, exact self/source-review pins and a specific clone-only authorization. It verifies original membership/pins, original negative closure, source-only catalog/partition, exact path-leaf census and full in-memory inverse checks before NEW.mkdir. The only two file-open sites use xb after that boundary; outputs and originals are reread, and the new directory must have exactly fifteen files without a grant or launch. It has no Main access, subprocess/native invocation or configuration-issuance path."
    },
    {
      "area": "Finite relocation scope",
      "finding": "Six members are selected for relocation: the metadata auditor, four subordinate JSON documents and preparation-review.json. The other nine members are byte-identical, including the complete matrix, strict driver and classifier. The planned twenty-eight JSON field coordinates are exact; eleven review paths plus five dependent length/hash pairs account for the review edit. Original JSON serialization and the one metadata source path inverse are verified here. Actual emitted JSON bytes, their per-step inverses and output pins remain deferred to separately authorized cloning and subsequent emitted-output review."
    },
    {
      "area": "Policy and observation separation",
      "finding": "The unchanged matrix preserves all 120 groups/2,051 source declarations, new3 order 18/8/12 and the disjoint 70-group/1,345-declaration partition. These are source declarations, not metadata predictions. The unchanged BQ constructor, strict driver and source outside the eleven edits preserve serial admission, 300-second initial grant freshness, 16 GiB memory and all positive source/artifact/process gates. Exact raw job and 100 ns time handling helpers remain byte-identical; no timestamps or outcomes are synthesized."
    },
    {
      "area": "Fresh retry authority remains explicit",
      "finding": "The inert eleven-field configuration is not executable as issued authority: clone authorization is false and Root source review is null. A distinct issued copy may change only status, clone authorization and the exact Root review pin. A separate retry catalog/relocation acceptance must then bind the actual new preparation-review and independently reviewed clone output. Original CB6 and the original catalog peer retain their original scope and cannot alone attest to relocated bytes."
    },
    {
      "area": "Downstream readiness",
      "finding": "No canonical placement occurred in this review. The helper retains all seventeen unresolved actual-only slots, and its eventual execution requires a fresh terminal-positive BuildQuery plus actual independent metadata acceptance. A separate Root retry execution source review must bind unchanged BQ constructor 972E and new auditor A04C. Runtime source canonicals and the separate runtime review remain future steps; this packet grants no native execution."
    }
  ],
